# Hoopilot — Firebase web config (OPTIONAL).
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and paste the values from
#   Firebase console > Project settings > Your apps > Web app > SDK setup
# The `.env` file is gitignored. Never commit real values.
#
# LEAVING THIS UNSET IS A SUPPORTED CONFIGURATION. With no config the app runs
# exactly as it always has: no account, no network calls, every session, shot
# and stat in the on-device SQLite database. See docs/FIREBASE-SETUP.md.
#
# Expo inlines EXPO_PUBLIC_* into the bundle, so treat these as PUBLIC values —
# which they are: a Firebase web config identifies the project, it does not
# authorise anything. What protects the data is the Firestore security rules in
# docs/FIREBASE-SETUP.md. A service-account key or an admin credential must
# NEVER go in this file.
#
# There is deliberately no storage bucket here: Hoopilot uploads numeric
# records only, so the client is never handed a bucket it has no business
# writing to.

EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
